// Per-map enforcement of the game's limited map area (rules.limitMapArea, set by logic setMapArea).
//
// Background: the engine clamps units and pathfinding only for non-AI teams, so crux AI (and any
// client that ignores the dark zone) can physically walk outside the allowed rectangle.
// When a map is listed here, the plugin:
//   - clamps every unit (optionally only players, see clampAI) to limitX/Y/Width/Height each tick;
//   - blocks place/break/rotate/configure actions outside the area.
// Darkness rendering itself is client-side and cannot be enforced by a server plugin.
// Fog of war (rules.fog) is not a movement boundary: the black around a fog map is visibility,
// not the limit; only the limitX/Y/Width/Height rectangle is enforced here.
//
// enabled: false    - disable the guard everywhere, even on listed maps.
// all: true         - apply to every map, ignoring the list below.
// clampAI: true     - also clamp AI units (crux). false = only player-controlled units.
// maps              - map file names (without .msav) or in-game display names, case-insensitive.
//                     Empty list = guard inactive. Add only maps that actually use limitMapArea.
{
    enabled: true
    all: false
    clampAI: true
    maps: [
        "archipelago"
        "lab"
    ]
}
